2-3. It followed the Declaration of Independence. ~ WAR
4-5. Displayed by Washington's soldiers. ~ VALOR
6-7. Fourth of July celebrations are not complete without these. ~ PARADES
8-9. The American eagle. ~ BIRD
10-11. What everybody does at a fourth of July banquet. ~ EATS
12-13. What orators will be on the fourth. ~ BUSY
14-15. What tired marchers will feel ready to do after a long parade. ~ DROP
16-17. One kind. ~ SORT
18-19. An inspiration. ~ IDEA
21-22. In a little while. ~ ANON
23-24. To mark off distances from point to point. ~ SPAN
25-26. To slash. ~ SLIT
27-28. What a person does in instituting legal proceedings against another. ~ SUES
29-30. What the American eagle does on the fourth of July. ~ SCREAMS
31-32. Eagles. ~ EARNS
33-34. Something good to eat. ~ PIE
1-20. A festivity. ~ GALA
2-9. To keep in safety. ~ WARD
4-13. To change. ~ VARY
6-29. What we mustn't shoot off in New York City on July 4. ~ PISTOLS
8-25. What a firecracker does if you hold it too long. ~ BURNS
12-21. A neck wrap worn by women. ~ BOA
3-10. What Paul Revere did. ~ RODE
5-14. What the Declaration of Independence is on every fourth. ~ READ
7-30. Displayed on every U. S. flag. ~ STRIPES
11-28. Swallowed by millions on the fourth. ~ SODAS
15-24. Used in signing the Declaration of Independence. ~ PEN
22-31. What we hope the weather will be on July 4. ~ NICE
26-33. What Washington caught Cornwallis in. ~ TRAP
35-36. Beloved by every Irishman. ~ ERIN
27-34. The kind of celebration New York has every fourth. ~ SANE
23-32. What the American school boys need not do on the fourth of July. ~ SUMS



